The NVRAM's matching is skipped too

Run 577's panel said w8m40: the matching thread is inside the name
comparison of the passive match, which takes the nub's own registry lock.
Somebody holds that lock and does not let go, so the thread never comes
back -- and the root nub's matching, the one our platform personality
belongs to, is behind it in the queue and never comes round.  That is why
the board has made no progress for so long: not our personality, not the
name, but a queue that never gets to us.

The NVRAM service's matching is the one it is stuck in.  The service is
called options-common, its driver is an Apple one this kernelcache does
not need, and the board reads its boot arguments from the device tree.
So its matching is skipped the way the other two are.

Skipping is reversible: the names are in one list, and the panel says
which one was skipped.

